if look around, nest js will be one of the main frameworks that we will be working with (maybe raw express will be in some apis)

but what we see now, moving generic nestjs <-> infrastructure parts of application to libs/api will be a benefit for future microservices

things like exepction filter, logger, access log interceptor

those are nestjs specific parts of configuration, but with them inside libs api we will have a raw implementaiton of it (that we already have in libs api) and also the adapters (for nestjs) in a reusable place

so lets analyze and extract those into some nestjs folder in libs api so that in future if other microservice would also want to use nestjs it would have all things to instantiate and use immediately



same with transactional typeorm module and persistence typeorm adatters for nestjs. those can also be moved to libs api

=====
after nest v12

vitest will be used + ESM

migrate completely to vitest for web and api
migrate completely to esm for web and api

remove completely jest from project
remove completely cjs commonjs etc from a project